---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout
  title="Native Tab Groups, Mirrored — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How cntxt mirrors Projects and Groups onto the browser's own native tab groups, in both directions."
  path="/learn/tab-groups"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Native tab groups, mirrored</h1>
  <p>
    cntxt mirrors Projects and Groups onto the browser's own native tab
    groups — in both directions. A Project or Group's live tabs show up as a
    real browser tab group with a matching title and color, so the browser's
    own UI already shows the same organization cntxt is tracking.
  </p>
  <p>
    It also works the other way: grouping tabs the normal, native way inside
    a Project's window silently becomes a nested Group — no cntxt-specific
    step required. You can even teach a recurring group (by title and color)
    to always file into a specific Project automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Mirror a Group's or Project's tabs into a native tab group</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>A new native group inside a Project's window becomes a nested Group automatically</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Teach a group's title/color to always file into a Project</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Rule management (list, edit, delete an existing rule)</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Reverse color sync (a manual recolor in the browser updates the Group)</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>A second native group inside a standalone Group's window</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
